    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Our knowledge of the brittle-ductile rocks as a function of temperature, pressure, and other environmental parameters is primarily based on experimental data. It has been difficult to test experimentally derived deformation laws in nature, because the critical parameters that determine the rheology of rocks are often poorly constrained. The Sierra Nevadan faults and fault zones described in this study provide a natural laboratory for studying the brittle and/or ductile accommodation of strain that can be related to the local state of stress due to fault interaction.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
